**[P1] Missing supplementary groups in `syscall.Credential`**

When switching to a different user, it is critical to also set their supplementary groups. Otherwise, the process will lack necessary permissions that the user is expected to have (e.g., access to specific files or devices).

```suggestion
	groups, err := usr.GroupIds()
	if err != nil {
		return nil, nil, fmt.Errorf("get group ids for user %s: %w", usr.Username, err)
	}
	var supplementaryGroups []uint32
	for _, gidStr := range groups {
		gid, err := strconv.ParseUint(gidStr, 10, 32)
		if err != nil {
			return nil, nil, fmt.Errorf("parse supplementary gid %s: %w", gidStr, err)
		}
		supplementaryGroups = append(supplementaryGroups, uint32(gid))
	}

	cred := &syscall.Credential{
		Uid:    uint32(uid),
		Gid:    uint32(gid),
		Groups: supplementaryGroups,
	}
```

