**[P1] Potential panic during shutdown due to race condition.**

Copying the `subscribers` slice and then sending to channels outside the lock is unsafe because `Close()` can run concurrently, closing the channels and causing a panic on send. Holding the read lock during the fan-out loop is a safer approach.

```suggestion
	b.mu.RLock()
	defer b.mu.RUnlock()

	if b.subscribers == nil {
		return
	}

	for _, ch := range b.subscribers {
```

**[P1] Retry backoff blocks shutdown.**

Using `time.Sleep` in the retry loop prevents the goroutine from exiting promptly when the system is shutting down. This can lead to hanging processes. It is better to use a context-aware wait.

```suggestion
		if attempt < w.maxRetries {
			select {
			case <-ctx.Done():
				return
			case <-time.After(w.backoff * time.Duration(1<<attempt)):
			}
		}
```

