body:
Same issue as above: `completeCh` is only signaled via `OnExecuteComplete`, so error-only executions will always incur the full graceful shutdown timeout. Consider also signaling completion from `OnExecuteError` and using a `sync.Once` to make the close safe if multiple terminal hooks can fire.
```suggestion
	// completeCh is closed when a terminal hook fires (completion or error),
	// meaning the final SSE event has been written and flushed. We only wait
	// for this callback as a safety check and then return immediately to avoid
	// fixed tail latency.
	completeCh := make(chan struct{})
	var completeOnce sync.Once

	hooks := c.setServerEventsHandler(ctx)

	origComplete := hooks.OnExecuteComplete
	hooks.OnExecuteComplete = func(executionTime time.Duration) {
		if origComplete != nil {
			origComplete(executionTime)
		}
		completeOnce.Do(func() {
			close(completeCh)
		})
	}

	origError := hooks.OnExecuteError
	hooks.OnExecuteError = func(err error) {
		if origError != nil {
			origError(err)
		}
		completeOnce.Do(func() {
			close(completeCh)
		})
	}
```

